SoXt: draw new scenes through the back buffer by default

On an expose or a new scene, SoXtRenderArea drew the first frame straight
into GL_FRONT and only glFlush'ed it, a workaround for old SGI graphics
hardware. libx11-compat composites a GLX window when it is swapped, so that
frame never reached the screen (a black canvas until the next redraw).
Default enableDrawToFrontBuffer to FALSE so every frame is swapped;
setDrawToFrontBufferEnable(TRUE) still restores the old behavior.

diff --git a/libSoXt/src/SoXtGLWidget.c++ b/libSoXt/src/SoXtGLWidget.c++
index ff5dabe..9fc551f 100644
--- a/libSoXt/src/SoXtGLWidget.c++
+++ b/libSoXt/src/SoXtGLWidget.c++
@@ -168,8 +168,13 @@ SoXtGLWidget::SoXtGLWidget(
     glxSize.setValue(0, 0);
     borderSize = 0;
     waitForExpose = TRUE;
-    drawToFrontBuffer = TRUE; // used by RA to draw new scenes to front buffer
-    enableDrawToFrontBuffer = TRUE;
+    // libx11-compat composites a GLX window when it is swapped, so a frame
+    // drawn straight to the front buffer and only glFlush'ed never reaches the
+    // screen. Draw new scenes through the back buffer and swap (the front
+    // buffer path was a workaround for old SGI graphics hardware);
+    // setDrawToFrontBufferEnable(TRUE) still turns it back on.
+    drawToFrontBuffer = FALSE; // used by RA to draw new scenes to front buffer
+    enableDrawToFrontBuffer = FALSE;
     
     //
     // window attribute list
